        "original_id": "a8650498-2b5e-55a4-b3e9-ba76b899d43f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Flammang Schrank, Theodore Roosevelt\n- Places: New York, Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States\n- Roles: U.S. President, 26th President of the United States\n- Events: Attempted assassination of Theodore Roosevelt, Progressive Era\n- Topics: Republican Party, American politics\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Roosevelt Jr. was born on October 27, 1858, and later became an American statesman, author, explorer, soldier, naturalist, and reformer.\n- Theodore Roosevelt served as the 26th President of the United States from 1901 to 1909.\n- Theodore Roosevelt was a leader of the Republican Party and a driving force for the Progressive Era in the United States in the early 20th century.\n- John Flammang Schrank was born on March 5, 1876, and was a resident of New York.\n- On October 14, 1912, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, John Flammang Schrank attempted to assassinate former U.S. President Theodore Roosevelt.\n- John Flammang Schrank died on September 15, 1943.\n- Theodore Roosevelt died on January 6, 1919.",
